sci-misc/llama-cpp-9999 user patches (portage applies only *.patch / *.diff here)

Currently: NONE. Since 2026-11-10 the ::pwr ebuild (sci-misc/llama-cpp/llama-cpp-9999.ebuild,
a copy of ::stuff's with priority over it) carries the CUDA patch itself:
  files/llama-cpp-9999-cuda-fa-mma-q-dequant-pr30202.patch  (PR #30202, OPEN DRAFT,
  rebased on eb4e244be 2026-10-29; applied softly under USE=cuda - a hunk that stops
  applying only ewarns and the build goes on without the FA q-dequant kernel).
A copy of the same patch here would be applied a SECOND time by eapply_user and abort
the build. Put a patch in this directory only for something the ebuild does not carry,
and rot-check it before each 'pkgs':
  git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp /tmp/lc-check &&
  git -C /tmp/lc-check apply --check "$PWD/<patch>"

History: 0002 (MMQ OOB, issue #27792) retired 2026-10-16 - upstream PR #29941 + #29953.
The expert-cache patches 0001/0003 used on the nvhard host are opt-in and NOT shipped here.
